From d1956d2df8093e13be4ce9aee44f713993ad0caa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 15:19:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01022/11171] [outer-loop] Declutter repo root: archive 155
 scratch scripts + guard recurrence

The repo root had accumulated ~155 one-off agent/experiment scratch files
(probe*.py, check_*.py, ~120 ad-hoc test_*.py, append_*.py, fix_test*.py,
replace_*/update_*/parse_tasks/flatten_p01/..., + stale retirement_plan.md /
MILESTONE_PREREQS.md). None are imported anywhere; pytest testpaths is
tests/python+tests/integration so the root test_*.py were never in the suite.

- ARCHIVED (git mv, history preserved) -> legacy/root-scratch-2026-06/ (follows
  the existing legacy/ convention; never-prune).
- DELETED regenerable build artifacts: main.aux/log/out (LaTeX), vivado*.{jou,log}
  + clockInfo.txt (Vivado scratch; vivado* were already gitignored-but-on-disk).

RECURRENCE GUARD (.gitignore): `/*.py` (+ !conftest.py/!setup.py) makes git ignore
ALL root-level .py, so `git add -A` -- including the conductor's --no-verify commits,
which still honor .gitignore -- can no longer re-track root scratch. Real Python
lives in python/, scripts/, tests/. Also gitignored the LaTeX root artifacts.

Root now contains only legit files (README/CLAUDE/LICENSE/configs/research-*.yaml).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
